course: dictionary
lesson: 5447
title: A word from rubbish and recycling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some hard words explain themselves in the sentence around them. Look for a comma or the word «where» after the hard word, because that is often where the meaning is given. «What is not recycled often goes to landfill, a huge hole where rubbish is buried and slowly rots, giving off a gas called methane.» The words after the comma tell you what a landfill is.
explain: Landfill is a noun, so it names a thing. You can say a landfill, or landfills. Landfill can also name the rubbish itself, as in «keep food out of landfill». Phrases such as «sent to landfill» and «go to landfill» all mean rubbish that is buried and not recycled.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Old batteries go in a special bin so their chemicals stay out of a huge hole in the ground.» That still makes sense, so you have understood the word. Clues like rots and methane also show that landfill is a place where rubbish gets worse, not better.
fact: A landfill is a large hole or site in the ground where rubbish is buried.
fact: Landfill can also mean the rubbish that is buried in those places.
fact: Rubbish in a landfill rots without air, and bacteria make methane, a gas that warms the planet.
fact: Some landfills collect methane and use it to make electricity.
fact: Landfills fill up, and they can pollute soil and water, so we reduce, reuse and recycle.
exercise: «What is not recycled often goes to landfill, a huge hole where rubbish is buried.» What is a landfill? | A bin lorry that collects rubbish | *A huge hole where rubbish is buried | A shop that sells recycled goods | A special bin for old batteries
exercise: «Food rotting in a landfill gives off methane, a gas that warms the planet.» What does methane do? | It turns soil into metal | It makes food fresh for longer | It cools the planet | *It warms the planet
exercise: Which word means a large hole in the ground where rubbish is buried? | battery | *landfill | bin | recycling
test: «Batteries thrown in normal bins have started fires in bin lorries.» Why should old batteries go in a special bin? | So bin lorries become heavier and slower | *So their metals can be used again and their chemicals stay out of landfill | Because batteries are a kind of food | So they can be buried in a landfill for fun
test: Ella says landfill is a type of food. What is the best reply? | No, it is a kind of bin lorry | Yes, it rots and gives off methane | *No, it is a large hole in the ground where rubbish is buried | Yes, it is what we eat at lunch
exam: What does the word landfill mean? | A type of recycled food | A gas that cools the planet | A special bin for paper only | *A large hole or site in the ground where rubbish is buried
